# 1. Canonical composite mockups — Tier A

These nine images are the **primary visual source of truth**.

| File | What it shows | Implementation authority |
|---|---|---|
| `01_essay-entry__canonical.png` | Hero/frontispiece, headline, metadata, flowing author card + Executive Signal, start of sticky Reading Companion | Canonical page entry, two-pane proportions, dark theme, type scale, flow-vs-sticky behavior |
| `02_first-scroll__canonical.png` | First substantive scroll, pull quote, active section marker, first inline figure; author/Executive Signal are gone | Canonical mid-essay sidebar state and section-marker treatment |
| `03_artifact-partial-context__canonical.png` | Partial-width composition, expanded Contextual Note, Editorial Table, active colored left rule | Canonical split-composition and contextual-note pattern |
| `04_thread-focus__canonical.png` | Focused thread inspection mode with only Running Example + Thread Overview in right rail | Canonical Thread Focus mode and return-to-essay affordances |
| `05_evidence-focus__canonical.png` | Evidence inspection mode: receipt, supported claim, limitations, evidence guide + index | Canonical Evidence Focus mode; not an essay-page section layout |
| `06_figure-viewer__canonical.png` | Enlarged figure modal over prior context, caption/long description and return behavior | Canonical FigureViewer/modal visual treatment |
| `07_managed-variation-inline__canonical.png` | Inline three-way comparison: Update / Reconcile / Deliberate Pin | Canonical inline explanatory comparison; **not** a separate mode/page |
| `08_conclusion-reading-path__canonical.png` | Closing figure, conclusion, `WhereThisSits`, previous/current/next question | Canonical essay conclusion and guided reading-path treatment |
| `09_mobile-modes__canonical.png` | Mobile essay entry, contents, thread focus, evidence focus | Canonical responsive visual language, not a native-app design |

## Canonical page-state rules visible in Tier A

- **Essay View:** primary pane + sidebar. Author and Executive Signal are normal-flow entry components; deeper in the essay only Reading Companion remains sticky.
- **Thread Focus:** focused inspection surface. Sidebar = Running Example + Thread Overview only. No author card, Executive Signal, or article TOC.
- **Evidence Focus:** focused inspection surface. Sidebar = Evidence Guide + Receipt Index only.
- **FigureViewer:** overlay/modal on top of the immediate prior context, and Close returns to that exact context.
- **Managed Variation:** remains inline in the essay.
- **WhereThisSits:** distinct from ordinary breadcrumb/series navigation; it explains the conceptual reading path.

---

# 2. Rich component direction — Tier B

These are **secondary visual references**, deliberately retained because they often contain richer card/detail treatments than the canonical composite set.

Use them for:
- card depth, glow, icon sizing, borders, spacing, mini-diagram polish;
- detailed Thread Overview and Running Example styling;
- ReceiptDisclosure/evidence-card richness;
- FigureViewer caption/control richness;
- typographic rhythm inside a component.

Do **not** use them to override:
- which components appear in the sidebar at a given scroll depth;
- whether something is a page versus a modal/focus surface;
- essay/thread/evidence information architecture;
- any factual copy, metrics, versions, availability states, or receipts;
- the final mobile navigation model.

### Files

- `01_essay-entry__rich-concept.png` — favored neo-editorial visual density and polish.
- `02_first-scroll__rich-concept.png` — rich first-scroll / diagram treatment; sidebar hierarchy is superseded.
- `03_artifact-partial-context__rich-concept.png` — detailed MediaSplit, table, badges; Executive Signal persistence is superseded.
- `04_thread-deployment__rich-concept.png` — useful Running Example detail card and technical figure polish; use canonical Thread Focus composition instead.
- `05_thread-use-overview__rich-concept.png` — strongest visual inspiration for Thread Overview / selected beat / hold state; canonical mode/sidebar rules supersede surrounding page.
- `06_managed-variation__rich-concept.png` — strong visual language for the three-path comparison; canonical semantics and copy supersede it.
- `07_evidence-receipts__rich-concept.png` — excellent Evidence/Receipt styling; **all fabricated receipt content is non-authoritative**.
- `08_figure-viewer__rich-concept.png` — detailed FigureViewer controls, caption treatment, previous/next; canonical return-state contract supersedes unsupported controls.
- `09_conclusion__rich-concept.png` — useful architecture-card treatment; invented next-essay and outcome copy must not be used.
- `10_mobile__rich-concept.png` — visual inspiration for mobile surfaces; robot assistant/app-tab concepts are superseded.

---

# 3. V2 prototype markups — Tier C

`03_V2_PROTOTYPE_MARKUPS/` is the rendered prototype family from the current experience specification. It is less visually lush than Tier B but is more trustworthy for **state and interaction semantics**.

Use it to resolve questions like:
- when the right rail changes;
- how Contextual Notes collapse/expand;
- what Thread Focus vs standalone thread looks like;
- how Evidence Focus returns;
- what mobile sheet/focus layouts do;
- how the thread sequence maps to essay anchors.

If a Tier-A image is visually ambiguous, consult V2 markups and `06_SUPPORTING_HANDOFFS/CURRENT-EXPERIENCE-SPEC.md`.

---

# 4. V1 prototype markups — Tier D

`04_V1_PROTOTYPE_MARKUPS/` contains the earlier full reading-experience wireframes. Keep them for layout archaeology and additional states, especially the six thread beats and earlier mobile experiments.

They are **not** current authority when they conflict with V2 or Tier A.

---

# 5. Initial style variations — Tier E

These four early explorations are mood/idea references only.

- Dark editorial variation — useful typography and section treatment.
- Light editorial variation — useful example of inline components and breathing room.
- Storyboard/dashboard variation — useful source for storyboard density, not final IA.
- Neo-editorial favorite variation — the visual ancestor of the current canonical system.

Agents may borrow aesthetic details only if they preserve Tier-A composition and V2 semantics.

---

# 6. Inline technical figures are a separate authority

The essay's semantic technical figures are not replaced by these page mockups. Follow `06_SUPPORTING_HANDOFFS/INLINE-FIGURE-IMAGE-USAGE-HANDOFF.md` for the latest named technical assets and placement rules.

That handoff requires the six thread images to remain in order and adjacent to corresponding prose, followed by the managed-variation comparison and closing estate figures when relevant. The mockups show **containers and presentation**, while the inline-figure handoff governs **which technical image is actually inserted**.

---

# 7. Agent implementation checklist

Before calling the visual implementation sufficient:

- [ ] Entry resembles Tier-A `01` in hierarchy, width balance, typography, and spacing.
- [ ] Author + Executive Signal scroll away; they do not persist deep into the article.
- [ ] Reading Companion is the only sticky essay sidebar surface at depth.
- [ ] Active section uses the colored left rule/number treatment without layout shift.
- [ ] Contextual Note is authored marginal context, not chat/AI generation.
- [ ] Dense figures can use primary-pane width and open in FigureViewer.
- [ ] Thread Focus contains only the focused beat plus Running Example + Thread Overview.
- [ ] Thread Focus has explicit `Back to essay` and `Read this scene in essay` semantics.
- [ ] Evidence Focus contains Evidence Guide + Receipt Index, not article TOC.
- [ ] Evidence content comes from real/source-grounded records; generated placeholders are not copied.
- [ ] Managed Variation is inline, not a modal/page.
- [ ] WhereThisSits remains a reading-path component, distinct from series/breadcrumb navigation.
- [ ] Mobile surfaces remain mobile web; no fabricated native-app tab bar/chatbot.
- [ ] FigureViewer returns to the immediate prior context and restores focus.
- [ ] Technical thread images follow the separate canonical image handoff.
- [ ] Actual current MDX/spec/evidence wins over text shown inside any generated mockup.

