111:### ContextualNote contract
112-
113:`ContextualNote` is a short, explicitly authored annotation keyed to `sectionId` or `sceneId`. It is not dynamically invented and makes no model call. It can explain a distinction, define a term, or note an evidence limit. Its expanded content should remain short; lengthy content belongs in the essay or Evidence Focus.
114-
115-Example mapping:
--
125-No note is required in every section. No blank card is reserved when none exists. “Dismiss” applies to that note ID for the current visit. “Collapse” applies to its detail; a dismissed note does not immediately reopen on another scroll event. Optionally offer a reader preference to hide all context notes.
126-
127:Switch notes only when the active semantic section changes, not at every paragraph or pixel. Pause replacement while focus is inside the note/companion or an overlay is open. Do not automatically expand a note. Mobile renders useful note content as an inline disclosure near the relevant text or under Contents—not floating over paragraphs.
128-
129:### ThreadDock contract
130-
131:Manual collapse takes precedence over proximity-triggered expansion. Holding a beat pins the **preview**, not the physical page or actual reading position. Display both when different: “Held preview: Use · Reading: Drift.” Default follow mode updates only sidebar context. It must never swap the inline canonical figure or automatically scroll the article.
132-
133-“Explore thread” opens the focused inspector for the selected or current beat. Focus mode has its own selected beat; it does not move the essay underneath. Keep the names **Incident, Deployment, Use, Drift, Detection, Outcome**.
--
176-A method summary must not masquerade as raw output. A code-like panel is permitted for **actual supplied captures** or explicitly marked illustrative schemas, never a generated signature verifier presented as observed implementation. Missing source URL, commit or exact runtime identity stays missing. Do not invent `E-1023`, a plausible commit hash, an official report or a 90-day measured gain.
177-
178:Evidence label is not evidence quality. “Externally reported” means attributed, not validated by us. “Measured” requires a stated method and denominator; it does not automatically mean causal. “Implemented” is a separate maturity dimension, not a synonym for “Observed.” A green color alone may not collapse these distinctions.
179-
180-The prototype uses bounded manuscript method summaries, with their lack of primary captures shown in every record. No measured outcome improvement is included.
--
210-## 12. Mobile
211-
212:The visual language is achievable as responsive HTML/CSS. A native app or PWA is not required. Keep the hero crop, serif title, navy surfaces, touch-sized controls and bottom-sheet Contents treatment. Reject the mockup's fake Home/Library/Agents tab bar and AI assistant.
213-
214:Short navigation opens in a bottom sheet; long Thread/Evidence Focus uses the full viewport. A persistent top return control remains available. Use `100dvh` and safe-area padding; test dynamic browser chrome, orientation, on-screen keyboard, zoom and iOS scroll locking. Respect reduced motion. No automatic audio, parallax, swipe-only controls or interactions that require hover.
215-
216-The figure caption/textual explanation remains useful at mobile width. Technical art may require enlargement. Do not render all six raster labels at illegible size and call that responsive.
