60-A reviewer skill used across my projects was missing a mandatory guard, so I fixed it at the source: the `/.claude/skills/` directory in my most active project. My personal registry showed the fixed version. Inside the source repository, the reviewer (obviously) had the new instruction, but every other project on the machine loaded a deployed file copy, and that copy sat five days without the fix.[^drift]
--
140-The runtime executes. A skill shapes its behavior. Markdown instructions don't reason on their own, and a signed context pack doesn't enforce the permissions it describes.
141-
142:Instruction, Tool, Context and Governance are the static side: the things an agent draws on. Execution is the runtime topology that selects which of them a session actually loads, and Evidence is what that session leaves behind.
