165-**Deployment** is where I lost the thread. A file copy is a separate object. Updating its source doesn't update it, and a successful registration says nothing about the copy another project loads.
--
167-The remedy is a recorded, registry-driven deployment. No manual copy/paste, no symlink as a shortcut around the record. A symlink follows the source checkout as branches change, so it drifts with the branch instead of leaving stale bytes behind. Multiple git worktrees make this worse, as each checkout silently maintains its own artifact state. Either way, “it's the same skill” conceals the state that matters.
