171-I need three separate answers: what the project intended to use, what is present on disk, and what the runtime actually used. A deployment check can establish the second without establishing the third. If a session started before the update, inspecting the file afterward won't tell me what it loaded. The run needs its own observation; absent that, the loaded version stays unknown.
